[game-contract] Define the target-neutral GamePackage and HostContract (complete)
Files: proposals/target-factory.md; proposals/presentation-host.md; crates/engine-api/**; crates/caravan-demo/**; crates/nworlds-desktop/**; crates/nworlds-host/**
Do: Inventory the concrete consumers that require host capabilities before naming any HostContract API. Separate game meaning, immutable state/query production, input interpretation, byte storage, lifecycle/resource access, and renderer-agnostic draw intent. Treat the current Caravan host ports and desktop wgpu proof as clients/evidence, not as the contract. Draft only the smallest consumer-shaped abstractions needed by the named consumers.
Accept: A consumer matrix names each required host capability, its consumer, its data direction, ownership, lifetime, and target-neutrality requirement; Worldline + LogicalTime -> GameState remains unchanged; GameState + Tau -> host-defined minimal RenderBatch remains the only render-production path; target metadata/device handles are absent from the game contract; and every unresolved API choice is recorded as a decision rather than silently selected.
> nworlds-host owns the target-neutral GamePackage runtime contract and independent InputIngress, RenderSink, StorageTransport, and PlatformInputAdapter ports; it has no Caravan or target dependency.
> GamePackage owns semantic control order: it ingests its package-defined input batch, performs interaction/publication/state selection/presentation, and returns one owned frame; the host only transports input, bytes, and frames.
> caravan-demo::CaravanPackage maps its existing Stage/Orchestrator/CaravanRenderer composition onto GamePackage; the desktop proof requests demo_package() and retains only native event and wgpu execution code.
@artifact text/plain crates/nworlds-host/src/lib.rs
@artifact text/markdown proposals/target-factory.md
