[composition] Define generated static target composition (complete)
Files: proposals/target-factory.md; proposals/presentation-host.md; .github/**; crates/**
Do: Specify whether nworlds generates a small static composition crate or selects a generic host executable, while keeping generated target details outside the game package and avoiding a plugin ABI in the first contract.
Accept: One composition mechanism is selected; the game package has no target entrypoint; generated composition owns target adapters; and the mechanism supports nworlds run and nworlds package.
-> game-contract
-> package-declaration
-> render-batch
> nworlds generates one ordinary Rust static composition crate per resolved package/profile operation; the generated crate owns target main, lifecycle, input translation, storage transport, and render execution around a GamePackage.
> A game package contains no target entrypoint or target adapter; generated target detail remains outside the package source tree.
> The generated composition supports Caravan and voxel clients through generic types and ports, never through a game-name branch in target execution.
