[cli] Define target-neutral nworlds commands (complete)
Files: proposals/target-factory.md; README.md; CONTRIBUTING.md
Do: Specify the user-visible behavior of nworlds test, nworlds run, and nworlds package, including package discovery, local artifact caching, failures, logs, and target transparency.
Accept: Normal game development requires no target flag or platform knowledge; commands map to the factory contract; and raw target commands remain internal maintenance/debug interfaces rather than public game workflow.
-> composition
-> package-declaration
-> resolution
> `nworlds test`, `nworlds run`, and `nworlds package` are the public commands; raw target/profile commands remain maintenance/debug interfaces.
> Discovery starts from a project root or explicit package source selector and requires exactly one loadable `PackageDeclaration`; source selection, test filters, verbosity, and output paths are not target selection.
> `nworlds test` validates semantic package evidence without selecting a target or minting a distributable artifact; `nworlds run` resolves local capabilities and launches a reused or minted artifact; `nworlds package` mints/reuses artifacts allowed by host/distribution policy.
> Stable host phases are discover, validate, resolve, artifact, and launch; failures preserve discovery, validation, resolution, artifact, or launch ownership, and unsupported resolution reports required, available, and remediation data.
---
[artifact-ci] Define TargetArtifact and CI evidence (complete)
Files: proposals/target-factory.md; proposals/platform-support-matrix.md; support.vine; .github/**; evidence/**
Do: Specify artifact identity, naming, metadata, checksums, retention, build checks, runtime evidence, device evidence, and publication behavior for supported profiles.
Accept: Each artifact maps to one resolved profile; compile, runtime, and device evidence are distinct; CI can mint supported artifacts without game-specific target code; and the support matrix remains host-owned.
-> cli
-> resolution
> Each TargetArtifact is immutable and maps to one package source/declaration and one resolved TargetProfile; its manifest records package/source/declaration digests, profile, generator/host contract, toolchain/build inputs, format, checksum, and evidence references.
> Local cache reuse and distribution retention are host-owned and checksum-verified; artifact naming may expose profile metadata to host/distribution tooling but never changes the package contract.
> Compile, runtime, and device evidence are separate claims; CI may mint and inspect artifacts without importing Caravan, voxel, or other application types into target-host production code, and compile-only evidence cannot close a runtime/device support row.
