Accept: No current proof detail is silently promoted to the target-factory contract; no game package contains target selection; the migration has one owner and acceptance path; and the target-local proof client remains independently buildable while the factory boundary is settled.
-> artifact-ci
-> cli
-> composition
-> game-contract
-> render-batch
-> resolution
> `nworlds-desktop` is classified as the current Caravan desktop proof client until the generic target-host contract and implementation are complete.
> Existing proof behavior is evidence to preserve, not API authority to promote; migration has one owner and cannot widen the game package contract.
> The gate is closed until RenderBatch, static composition, and resolution decisions are complete.
