[desktop-host-contract] Define reusable desktop target composition (complete)
Files: proposals/target-factory.md; proposals/presentation-host.md; crates/nworlds-host/**; crates/nworlds-desktop/**; crates/engine-presentation/**; .github/**
Do: Specify the target-neutral desktop composition around `GamePackage`, `InputIngress`, `PlatformInputAdapter`, `StorageTransport`, and `RenderSink<Frame<RenderBatch>>`. Decide which lifecycle, resize, shutdown, surface/device, and frame scheduling responsibilities belong to the reusable desktop host and which values are supplied by a package client.
Accept: The contract can host both Caravan and voxel packages; the desktop composition owns native lifecycle and backend execution; package clients supply semantic input vocabulary and `RenderBatch` production; no target entrypoint imports Caravan, voxel, or a game-domain type; and the first composition remains ordinary static Rust.
-> composition
-> render-batch
-> resolution
> `nworlds-desktop` is a reusable generic target host/composition around `GamePackage` and package-neutral ports; it is not a Caravan library.
> The target host owns `winit`/`wgpu` lifecycle, resize, surface-loss, shutdown, and redraw scheduling; it never selects worldlines, interprets facts, assigns logical time, or inspects package state.
> Generated compositions supply package-defined input packets/adapters and `GameState + Tau -> Frame<RenderBatch>` production; the host consumes only `InputIngress`, `StorageTransport`, and `RenderSink<Frame<RenderBatch>>` ports.
