Files: crates/nworlds-desktop/**; crates/nworlds-host/**; Cargo.toml; Cargo.lock; .github/workflows/ci.yml
Do: Implement the settled static desktop composition and its synthetic-package tests. Move native lifecycle, event translation hooks, surface/device setup, resize/loss handling, and frame submission behind the target-neutral host boundary. Keep target-specific code independent of Caravan and voxel packages.
Accept: `nworlds-desktop` production dependencies contain no Caravan or voxel crate; a synthetic package can compile and submit an owned `Frame<RenderBatch>`; native lifecycle behavior remains target-local; the existing Windows proof can be remapped without changing engine semantics; and CI has a target-host compile check.
-> artifact-ci
-> desktop-host-contract
-> game-contract
> The implementation must use static generics/composition, not runtime package discovery or a plugin ABI.
> Target-local errors, device handles, surfaces, and native event types terminate at the host boundary.
> The generic host is allowed to know `RenderBatch`; it is forbidden to know `Snapshot`, `RenderOutput`, `VoxelState`, `CaravanPackage`, or any game fact type.
