[desktop-evidence] Prove generic desktop composition and client preservation (planning)
Files: crates/purity-tests/**; crates/nworlds-host/**; crates/nworlds-desktop/**; crates/caravan-demo/**; crates/voxel-sample/**; evidence/**; .github/workflows/**
Do: Add synthetic-package host evidence, target-host dependency guards, Caravan client regression evidence, voxel client regression evidence, native compile/runtime evidence, and explicit compile/runtime/device status distinctions. Keep native visual evidence target-local and preserve workspace/conformance/purity/CodeQL checks.
Accept: Generic desktop host tests run without Caravan or voxel packages; both clients build through the same composition; target dependency guards pass; native compile and runtime evidence are separately named; no engine or host contract gained game-specific types; and the target-factory migration gate can close.
-> artifact-ci
-> desktop-target-closure
-> migration-gate
> Synthetic package evidence proves genericity; Caravan/voxel evidence proves client preservation; neither evidence class is allowed to stand in for the other.
> Compile success is not runtime support, and desktop runtime success is not device/profile support.
> The host contract remains scheduler-independent and never turns host time into logical game time.
